  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Turnover Bridge. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Turnover Bridge is a 2-player trick game (more related to Whist than Bridge). 52-card deck, 26 each. Layout: 12 face-down in row + 12 face-up on top + 2 secret hole cards. Spades permanently trump. Play face-up cards or hole cards. When face-up played, turn over card beneath. Win 14+ of 26 tricks. Information warfare: visible cards vs hidden cards.',
    objective: 'Win 14 or more of the 26 tricks. Spades are permanent trump. Players use a 12+12+2 layout (12 face-down, 12 face-up on top, 2 hole cards); when a face-up card is played, the card beneath is turned over and becomes available.',
    gameplay: 'Play any face-up card or hole card. Follow suit. Trump with spades if void. When face-up card played, turn over card beneath (now available). 2 hole cards kept secret. Highest trump or highest led suit wins trick.',
